================================================================================
TrailDiscover — Adan Alvarez
================================================================================

Used in: companion/data/tags.yaml (the "TrailDiscover — AWS operations seen in the
         wild (#2345)" section, rules td_aws_*)

TrailDiscover (https://github.com/adanalvarez/TrailDiscover) is a catalogue of AWS
CloudTrail events with their MITRE ATT&CK techniques and whether each has been
used in the wild. Its data is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International licence (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

Material used: from events/<Service>/<Event>.json at upstream commit
78156accdf5b6c325100ddb64c5300586f67079c, the event names and sources, the
"usedInWild" flag and the ATT&CK technique identifiers. Changes made: the events
were filtered (only those used in the wild, and only those no other rule in this
program already grades), grouped into tagger rules, and given severities and
conditions that are this program's own judgment, not TrailDiscover's. No
descriptions, incident texts or other prose from TrailDiscover are included.
TrailDiscover's author does not endorse this program.


